; it was corrected by changing the private directory to root:www-data mode 0750, and the final snapshots show no failed units, healthy package state, and only the required 8443 listener. The transient fault left no observed residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b96a47aaaea2462a","cmd-2e38920b189a4b67","cmd-a9a91c6d78394b27","cmd-4abaa08f132642e7","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and direct recovery checks for trust, certificate material, HTTPS service, content, and remote connectivity.","limitations":["Lifecycle snapshots inventory general system health, sockets, temporary files, and package consistency but do not independently inventory certificate files or trust-store contents; those final states are established by executor commands.","The HTTPS service briefly entered an auto-restart loop because its runtime user could not traverse the private-key directory. Evidence shows this was corrected before final validation and restart testing."]}
